2.1631.803However, element 42 is a patch that is attached to the patient's body at a specific position, e.g. typically by an adhesive. See Derkx, paragraphs [0063] & [0064]. Derkx does not describe a "a carrier configured to fit, while in use, fully around the human body, at an abdominal part thereof." (Emphasis added). Derkx, lacking the "fully around" aspect of Applicant's claimed invention, includes an adhesive to enable the patch 42 to remain in place.

